{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Answered</b>: The sense is, [he answered] concerning the haste of the harshness. Then Arioch informed Daniel that he should come and request time for himself, and so he did. And Daniel came and requested from the king, in the language of the Holy Tongue: <b>if you seek, seek it</b> [אם תבעיון בעיו]."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes the Aramaic of the verse (אם תבעיון בעיו) and calls it 'the language of the Holy Tongue,' referring to its scriptural Aramaic form. The phrase טעם מהחצפה מהירות is compressed; rendered hyper-literally as 'the sense is concerning the haste of the harshness.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:11.049737941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}